/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H2Piz-formation.dat -- the first 2 protonations of piperazine, written from the master:
      Piz + 2 H+  <=>  H2Piz
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 5.333, dH1 = 31.11 kJ/mol, dCp 86 J/mol/K (grade AAB)
      pK2 = 9.731, dH2 = 42.89 kJ/mol, dCp 75 J/mol/K (grade AAB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is Piz, the form a case declares; this record carries steps 1 to 2 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  The neutral base is a different object from the catalogue component of the same substance (monoethanolamine, diethanolamine, triethanolamine, triethylamine, methylamine, piperazine exist as components); no gas-liquid record links this species to it, so the dissolved base and the component are two identities until one is written.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H2Piz; masters ( { ion Piz; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 2; } );
      logK25 15.064; dH -74000; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.53, p. 329: pK1 5.333, dH1 31.11 kJ/mol, pK2 9.731, dH2 42.89 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
